rol point to ensure that any third-party involvement adheres to Brazilian data protection principles. [Data: Relationships (368, 365, 366, 369, 370); Entities (375, 376, 372, 367, 368 +more)].\\n\\nThe presence of Transferencia a Terceiros (375) as a listed entity, together with the regulatory directive in the REGULATORIA relationship to TRANSFERENCIA A TERCEIROS (368), indicates a formal obligation to align third-party data handling with LGPD. This combination elevates compliance risk for vendors and partnering entities if LGPD requirements are not properly operationalized. [Data: Relationships (368, 365, 366, 369, 370)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Controller-exclusive data usage and third-party access restrictions\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Data usage is restricted to the controller (Art. 16 IV), with third-party access prohibited and data to be anonymized when shared, signaling strict control over data access and transformation. This mechanism is defined by USO EXCLUSIVO DO CONTROLADOR (376) and reinforced by the REGULATORIA relationship to USO EXCLUSIVO DO CONTROLADOR (369). [Data: Entities (372, 367, 368, 375, 376 +more); Relationships (369, 365, 366 +more)].\\n\\nThis framework aims to minimize exposure risk by ensuring that only authorized parties within a defined scope can interact with payroll data, and that sharing occurs under anonymization where appropriate. The explicit restriction on third-party access reduces the potential surface for data misuse but also imposes vendor onboarding and technical controls to maintain compliance. [Data: Relationships (369, 365, 366)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Four retention exceptions under Article 16\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The framework acknowledges four retention exceptions under Article 16, codified as Quatro Exceções de Conservacao ART16 (377) and described in the REGULATORIA context (370). These exceptions delineate when retention obligations may be modified or shortened, providing 